  era: "Section 3 \xB7 Vedic Period \xB7 c. 1500 \u2013 600 BCE"
  title: Who were the Aryans?
  text: In the Rigveda, arya means noble, a cultural and linguistic term. Most scholars hold that Indo-Aryan-speaking groups migrated into north-west India around 1500 BCE and mixed with local peoples; others argue for an indigenous origin. The debate continues.
